# The secrets accessor's bench backend. NEVER committed — see env-source.sh.
.secrets
# The instance's own configuration, copied from .env.example and edited per box.
.env
node_modules/
node_modules/

# ⚠️ THAT PATTERN IS WHY `apps/<id>/node_modules/` NEEDS NO LINE OF ITS OWN, and it is load-bearing since
# pk24/D3: `bin/instance-app.guard.mjs` writes a symlink farm there (the app's declared dependencies, out of
# a Forge checkout) so this box's own apps can be compiled and tested where they live. It is rewritten on
# every run, `bin/build-local.sh` copies apps to the oven with `--exclude node_modules`, and nothing in it may
# ever be committed: every link points into a checkout on THIS machine.

# The Forge tarballs `bin/vendor-packages.sh` builds from a monorepo checkout. Build output, megabytes of
# it, whose source of truth is that repository — committing them would make this the second place a package
# version lives. `@forgeco/*` reached npm on 16/09, so what keeps them here is no longer the registry but
# the box: these images are baked from a CHECKOUT, not from a release. See bin/vendor-packages.sh.
storefront-coffee/vendor/
# The vitrine's build output.
storefront-coffee/.next/
storefront-coffee/next-env.d.ts
storefront-coffee/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# The same tarballs, for the counter's kiosk. `bin/vendor-packages.sh <forge checkout> totem` writes them and
# `totem/` installs from them — same pre-release mechanism as the vitrine above, same reason they stay out.
totem/vendor/
# The totem's build output.
totem/.next/
totem/next-env.d.ts
totem/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# GENERATED by bin/box-up.sh (step 3c) from the café store id — a fresh ULID on every birth.
# A committed copy is correct for one box and a lie for every other. The shape lives in
# caddy/extra-local/coffee.caddy.example, whose name no import matches.
#
# ⚠️ THE FOLDER IS `extra-local/` AND NOT `extra/` (A10): `caddy/Caddyfile` imports `extra/*.caddy` at TOP
# level, where a file is a SITE BLOCK, and this one is a FRAGMENT read from inside the bench's site block.
# `*.caddy` matches `coffee.local.caddy`, so the two globs over one folder killed the production edge
# outright. See caddy/extra-local/README.md and bin/caddy-extra-door.guard.mjs.
caddy/extra-local/coffee.caddy

# ★★ WHAT A RED RUN LEFT BEHIND — container logs copied out by `capture_evidence` in bin/box-up.sh before
# anything could recreate them. Never committed: a kernel log carries tokens, hostnames and buyer data.
postmortem/

# ★ ONE LOG PER RUN OF `bin/box-cycle.sh`, plus its lock. A ~90-minute cycle has no terminal, so its
# whole transcript lands here — kernel addresses, hostnames and the tail of a seed included. Never committed,
# for the same reason `postmortem/` is not.
cycle-logs/
